  "notes": {
    "1-3": "Single cucumber leaf proposals visually reviewed; frame-cropped examples9c866d271fda2d797399/2ee9139f6a1b6e00c777 need explicit truncation policy.",
    "4-7": "Single cucumber lamina plus small petiole; boxes generally follow leaf. Frame-edge proposals remain explicit review flags, not automatic rejection. No diagnosis inferred visually.",
    "8-11": "Single cucumber N/N_K lamina, folds retained; reviewed visible boxes. Edge-truncated6d3d257f9109ac65705 explicitly stays flagged. Disease/deficiency labels are author-derived, no photo-based reassignment.",
    "12-15": "Cucumber N_K and healthy: numerous healthy closeups have real truncated frame boundaries; do not mistake automatic frame flags for segmentation corruption. Explicit visible-leaf bbox policy needed; labels preserved from publisher.",
    "16-19": "Cucumber healthy ends; tomato JAS_MIT/K leaflets begin. Some attached smaller leaflets: area_extreme0521c382a546ec88afbe is real tiny visible leaflet, not mask failure. Additional visible leaflets outside chosen main box require multi-object/compound-leaf decision, e.g92ebe68ed32363714d92; no acceptance yet.",
    "20-23": "Tomato K then LM: visible main lamina boxes generally follow extent; curled leaflets need no invented expanded tissue. Small attached lateral leaflets remain explicit ambiguity (compound versus multiple annotations). No visual disease inference.",
    "24-27": "Tomato LM single visible main leaf/leaflet extent reviewed. Small lateral laminae connected to petiole often included within proposal; exhaustive small-object policy still pending. Frame flagged07df65b6e65722b343bc has actual petiole to edge.",
    "28-31": "Remaining LM proposals: dark necrotic lamina retained rather than bounding pale lesion only. Petiole/connected minor leaflets sometimes expand box; no obvious cloth-dominated box on these sheets. Need fullresolution multi-leaf correction where applicable.",
    "32-35": "LM final / MIT begins: connected small leaflets are consistently a target-definition issue, e.gdee0fbd6f44a1d4b90e7 (LM) andbfb0e2455bb7fa3ba2b0 (MIT). Most isolated leaflet proposals good at preview resolution; no mask-only acceptance.",
    "36-39": "MIT photos: mainly isolated main leaflet with small lateral laminae/petioles. Boxes capture visible plant extent, not background. Many opposite-face/pose similarities possible; all originals cannot be asserted independent physical leaves.",
    "40-43": "MIT majority bbox extent valid in preview. c08c96868bfcd373a410 shows two distinct comparable leaflets connected by stem, so one-box proposal must not be accepted as an isolated leaflet without correction.6fa3022fb6ec8a8f1eee has several lateral laminae; require final object policy.",
    "44-47": "MIT ends / tomato N begins. Larger multi-lamina examplesd2f914167fe2cd798652/7c776291e876cf356ca8 need correction. Tomato N grey/lighter cloth versus darker MIT is source/background confounding, not a new independent field diagnostic evaluation.",
    "48-51": "N/N_K small frames accurately contain visible tissue; area-extreme6d782d6668fb0f5ba5d7/626b98dafceab7d45dd0/73afa613790ae9dfe2ad are genuinely small objects. Healthy begins; visual appearance alone does not override source healthy annotation.",
    "52-55": "Author-labeled healthy tomato samples: primary-lamina boxes generally follow the visible object, but 6094986e4124b920597e/ecb7588f0e2ecc3901ba/60c1c9abee9b022cb118/3146c7b454e5eaa8c6bf show attached side leaflets that need a consistent compound versus individual-lamina contract. Do not relabel healthy from visual symptoms. d7de1d4f5f436c916c43 has an isolated white background fleck outside the box, not another leaf.",
    "56-59": "Healthy tomato: boxes follow visible green material, with several connected compound samples (e.g. 7e6a13e9e2c9c5a257ae, 68f51b8964e1139faae4, 43f6e0c13ad93e749660, b72cd4cc1c90d6fa843c). Thin petioles and small leaflets require an explicit leaf-sample target contract; no obvious cloth-dominated bbox. Repeated dorsal/ventral appearances cannot establish independent physical plants.",
    "60-63": "Healthy tomato proposals continue to follow leaf samples, including attached leaflets. Tiny real samples 84c9064be8436849a211 and 74af0ecf339f583b9a41 illustrate that area_extreme alone is not rejection. No disease diagnosis inferred from appearance; retain source labels and resolve sample-unit geometry before training.",
    "64-66": "Final healthy tomato sheets: main leaf and attached small lateral laminae are visible in several source samples, including 351f293d31d482cf8c3e and 02044af61584ec8da021. Bboxes generally include the sample rather than cloth; this does not resolve physical grouping or full-original geometry. All 1047 rendered proposals have now actually been visually seen, without accepting training labels."
